From ba81a97c12e562ecda9961b568f3f9c42f53ce9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:50:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-109: a property marker on every row; its menu
 jumps to the HTML too (0.109.0)

WPF puts a property marker right of every property value. Here only the rows
the .dfm gives had one, and its menu had only Reset. Now every row has one
(fainter where nothing is compared: the .dfm does not give it, a system colour,
several selected with different values), and the menu is Reset + "to the HTML
source" (the same as a double-click on the name). A right-click on the row opens
the same menu (in a text field it stays the field's own cut / copy / paste).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 187, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (a marker on every row, 4 faint; Top's menu with Reset off -> revealProp:Top;
right-click on Width -> revealProp:Width; no menu from a right-click in a text field).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
